ealed predictions", "phase": 1, "track": "methods", "priority": "high", "requires_gpu": false, "max_turns": 100, "estimated_wall_time_min": 45, "per_unit_rows": true, "milestone": "2026.10.720", "deliverable": "results/experiment_8346_v720_frozen_input_contract.json", "inference_substrate_class": "no_model_load", "MODEL_SPECS": [], "gated_on": [], "prior_failures": [{"experiment_id": "exp8318-contract-replay", "verdict": "complete_disqualified_contract_replay", "addressed_by": "Use the now-qualified Exp8332 replay controls. Reuse successful Exp8334/8335 outputs; current input qualification is scoped separately from historical failure.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}], "prompt": "CONTEXT:\nWork in {project_root} on {date}. V719 wrote nine producer primaries and three conductor pre-gate receipts; two producer slots have neither. Static heads and reserved predictions qualified (Exp8334/8335). Local qualification failed three Exp8206 consumer assertions; runtime failed two Exp8307 authority assertions; ARC failed strict typing; cost consumers failed three Exp8329 assertions. GateMate history drifted. The capstone passed its memory checks but failed two branch replays. H1/H2 remain unmeasured. Preserve the frozen V717 science and historical outcomes. Cached observations are exposed development, not current model inference.\nEXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:\nCLAUDE.md; CODEX.md; ops/e2e-test-plan.md; ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml; openspec/capabilities/research-reporting/spec.md; openspec/capabilities/verification/spec.md; scripts/experiment_template.py; python/carnot/reporting/primary_publication.py; openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md; openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-v719-preserved-20261009.md; openspec/change-proposals/v717-local-learning-protocol.json; python/carnot/reporting/roadmap_contract.py; results/experiment_8332_v719_contract_replay.json; results/experiment_8334_v719_sentence_spline_fit.json; results/experiment_8335_v719_reserved_prediction_seal.json; python/carnot/verify/sentence_spline_fit_8334.py; python/carnot/verify/reserved_prediction_seal_8335.py; research-studying.md; python/carnot/reporting/v717_capstone.py; python/carnot/reporting/v717_capstone_evidence.py; results/experiment_8317_v717_capstone.json; results/experiment_8304_v717_contract_methods.json; results/experiment_8305_v717_cached_sentence_custody.json; scripts/adversarial_verify.py; research-references.md; python/carnot/reporting/v718_contract_replay.py; python/carnot/reporting/v718_replay_history.py; python/carnot/reporting/v718_replay_runner.py; tests/python/test_v718_contract_replay_8318.py; results/experiment_8318_v718_contract_replay.json; openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-v718-preserved-20261009.md\nTASK:\nBind fourteen tasks and reuse qualified heads and sealed predictions. Deliver results/experiment_8346_v720_frozen_input_contract.json. Create the thin runner scripts/experiments/experiment_8346_v720_frozen_input_contract.py. Store primitive evidence under results/raw/experiment_8346_v720_frozen_input_contract/. Future deliverables are dependencies, not existing inputs.\nCONCRETE STEPS:\n1. PRECONDITIONS: Emit a flushed start line. Authenticate source bytes, terminal sidecars and task authority. Check private scratch, tools and resources before work. Name missing external operands in gate_check_summary. Do not replace natural evidence with fixtures.\n2. Emit a flushed progress line at every phase boundary. Emit one before and after every model load, generation, benchmark and subprocess. Print completed/pending counts inside long loops. Poll owned children at least every 60 seconds. Use unbuffered output and bounded deadlines. Keep every silence gap below 600 seconds. Write files over about 200 lines in several tool calls of at most about 150 lines. Send a progress message between calls. No single huge tool call. Do not pad elapsed time.\n3. Spec first: add relevant REQ-* and SCENARIO-* before implementation. Write focused failing tests first. Reuse existing modules through small adapters. Preserve assertions, guard thresholds and old evidence. Keep scratch in /tmp and runners in scripts/experiments/. Do not modify research-roadmap.yaml. Freeze validation commands before measurement.\n4. Declare no_model_load, MODEL_SPECS=[] and zero current model calls. Identify cached verifier work or artifact aggregation as the inference_substrate. Training small numeric heads is not an LLM load.\n5. Compare the V720 visible table, complete JSON task objects and YAML. Bind activated authority only after activation. Preserve V719 snapshots and immutable V717 protocol bytes. This is the milestone manifest task, not permission to activate a roadmap.\n6. Reuse Exp8332 source-custody controls. Authenticate Exp8305 predictor/evaluator shard hashes, Exp8334 heads and Exp8335 prediction seals directly. Do not refit, regenerate predictions or open reserved labels. Historical disqualified tasks cannot supply a readiness bit. Report separate frozen_heads_ready_score and frozen_predictions_ready_score so a failed history audit cannot suppress authentic inputs.\n7. Recount original roles: fit128, tune32/32, reserved128 split stream96/retention32. Expected usable counts are 104 labeled fit, 25 calibration, 28 selection, 97 reserved, 74 stream, 67 later and 23 retention. Preserve missing slots and both transport/feature counts. Require the unchanged V717 role/support rules. Freeze exact checkpoint, selected comparator, temperatures, action rules and all method hashes.\n8. Ingest the V720 reference scan before execution. Read full methods for 2602.02056v4, 2512.12850v3 and 2606.11711v1. Bind source URLs, versions, local hashes, assumptions and limits in docs/research-notes/v720-method-ingestion.md. Update research-studying.md with adoption/defer decisions. Lookup-table fidelity and finite feedback capacity are separate constructed studies; do not import their observations into H1/H2.\n9. Freeze a V720 execution manifest. Give historical consumers explicit immutable milestone and operand roots; never swap the live roadmap on disk. Require byte-bound positive and missing/drift controls. Static fitting and sealing have completed; replace them with authenticated reuse. Run private E2E-018 and verify changed/deleted task objects fail.\n10. Run relevant unit and consumer tests, scoped Ruff check/format, strict mypy and scripts/check_spec_coverage.py --files <owned-test-files>. Require 100 percent newly owned statements, including real CLI, child and failure paths. Use pytest -n 0 -o addopts= with private scratch. Record argv, exit, timing and log hashes. Do not run the full repository suite inside this experiment.\n11. Cold-replay primitive evidence in a fresh process. Run valid, negative and self-consistently rehashed tamper controls. Use unchanged primary_publication checks, scripts/adversarial_verify.py --json <private-candidate> and scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py --strict <private-candidate>. Keep all findings. An exit1 requires the existing typed finding consumer: only independently recomputed informational findings with deliberate-error controls can resolve. Errors, unknown severity, warnings and critical findings block readiness. Do not edit those validators or exemption lists. Publish the terminal primary atomically after checks. Owned failures are disqualified; unchanged external blocks are blocked, never partial. Reconcile openspec/, _bmad/traceability.md, ops/status.md and ops/changelog.md. Do not update generator weights or publish externally.\nREQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:\nexperiment_id, task_id, milestone, run_date: principle: Bind the invocation to its exact authority.\nhonest_verdict, verdict_class: principle: honest_verdict starts complete_. Class is positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial. Partial means retryable unfinished owned work only.\ngate_check_summary: principle: A block names upstream, path/hash, field, operator, expected and observed values. Missing is distinct from zero.\ninference_substrate, inference_substrate_class, MODEL_SPECS, model_invocation_counts, historical_model_provenance: principle: Separate current work from imported inference.\nrows, intended_count, completed_count, failed_count, censored_count, excluded_count, independent_count, sample_size_budget: principle: Retain every intended unit and condition. Repeated timings do not add independent sources.\nverifier_is_oracle, exposure_scope, independent_generalization_score, generalized_learning_benefit_score: principle: Oracle controls use circular_positive. Both generalization scores remain zero on exposed development.\nrequired_checks_passed, flagged_adversarial, acceptance_gates, validation_receipts, terminal_validation_sidecar_path, adversarial_findings: principle: Readiness requires byte-bound checks, not scientific success.\npreconditions_checked, duration_s, phase_spans, random_seed, reproducibility_checksum, source_artifact_hashes, code_config_hashes, raw_shard_hashes: principle: Bind claims to measured work and replayable inputs.\ncited_upstream_artifacts, field_principles: principle: List imported evidence and explain every added field.\ncurrent_contract_ready_score, frozen_heads_ready_score, frozen_predictions_ready_score, canonical_tasks_sha256: principle: Exact authority and each reusable input qualify separately.\nprotocol_path, protocol_sha256, input_receipts, role_counts, methods_manifest, execution_manifest: principle: Freeze science and inputs before evaluation.\nRun command: cd {project_root} && PYTHONPATH=python:. PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 .venv/bin/python -u scripts/experiments/experiment_8346_v720_frozen_input_contract.py --date {date}\nDo NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.", "model": "opus"}, {"id": "exp8347-local-consumer-qualification", "title": "Qualify local learning after isolating historical consumer operands", "phase": 1, "track": "infrastructure", "priority": "high", "requires_gpu": false, "max_turns": 100, "estimated_wall_time_min": 65, "per_unit_rows": true, "milestone": "2026.10.720", "deliverable": "results/experiment_8347_v720_local_consumer_qualification.json", "inference_substrate_class": "no_model_load", "MODEL_SPECS": [], "gated_on": [], "prior_failures": [{"experiment_id": "exp8306-local-update-isolation", "verdict": "complete_disqualified_owned_checks", "addressed_by": "The sole failed terminal command returned exit1 for an informational exact-zero metric. Preserve it; independently verify dense parity and qualify strict typed finding consumption with false-zero controls.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}, {"experiment_id": "exp8319-local-evidence-qualification", "verdict": "blocked_gate_check_failed", "addressed_by": "The kernel never ran: unrelated historical-reader readiness was zero. Remove that edge, authenticate this task directly, and test the existing finding consumer locally before the unchanged 48-trajectory numerical/restart study.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}, {"experiment_id": "exp8333-local-evidence-qualification", "verdict": "complete_disqualified_local_evidence_qualification", "addressed_by": "Exp8206 binds Exp8172 historical exclusion-manifest bytes to the mutable current manifest. Authenticate the old snapshot separately, retain current retirement enforcement, and pass every unchanged child/consumer assertion.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}], "prompt": "CONTEXT:\nWork in {project_root} on {date}. V719 wrote nine producer primaries and three conductor pre-gate receipts; two producer slots have neither. Static heads and reserved predictions qualified (Exp8334/8335). Local qualification failed three Exp8206 consumer assertions; runtime failed two Exp8307 authority assertions; ARC failed strict typing; cost consumers failed three Exp8329 assertions. GateMate history drifted. The capstone passed its memory checks but failed two branch replays. H1/H2 remain unmeasured. Preserve the frozen V717 science and historical outcomes. Cached observations are exposed development, not current model inference.\nEXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:\nCLAUDE.md; CODEX.md; ops/e2e-test-plan.md; ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml; openspec/capabilities/research-reporting/spec.md; openspec/capabilities/verification/spec.md; scripts/experiment_template.py; python/carnot/reporting/primary_publication.py; openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md; openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-v719-preserved-20261009.md; openspec/change-proposals/v717-local-learning-protocol.json; results/experiment_8333_v719_local_evidence_qualification.json; python/carnot/verify/local_qualification_8333.py; python/carnot/reporting/local_qualification_execution_8333.py; python/carnot/verify/hard_exit_learning_qualification_8206.py; tests/python/test_hard_exit_learning_qualification_8206.py; python/carnot/verify/local_update_isolation_8306.py; python/carnot/reporting/local_update_isolation_8306.py; python/carnot/reporting/local_update_execution_8306.py; tests/python/test_local_update_isolation_8306.py; results/experiment_8306_v717_local_update_isolation.json; python/carnot/reporting/v718_replay_history.py; results/experiment_8319_local_evidence_qualification.json\nTASK:\nQualify local learning after isolating historical consumer operands. Deliver results/experiment_8347_v720_local_consumer_qualification.json. Create the thin runner scripts/experiments/experiment_8347_v720_local_consumer_qualification.py. Store primitive evidence under results/raw/experiment_8347_v720_local_consumer_qualification/. Future deliverables are dependencies, not existing inputs.\nCONCRETE STEPS:\n1. PRECONDITIONS: Emit a flushed start line. Authenticate source bytes, terminal sidecars and task authority. Check private scratch, tools and resources before work. Name missing external operands in gate_check_summary. Do not replace natural evidence with fixtures.\n2. Emit a flushed progress line at every phase boundary. Emit one before and after every model load, generation, benchmark and subprocess. Print completed/pending counts inside long loops. Poll owned children at least every 60 seconds. Use unbuffered output and bounded deadlines. Keep every silence gap below 600 seconds. Write files over about 200 lines in several tool calls of at most about 150 lines. Send a progress message between calls. No single huge tool call. Do not pad elapsed time.\n3. Spec first: add relevant REQ-* and SCENARIO-* before implementation. Write focused failing tests first. Reuse existing modules through small adapters. Preserve assertions, guard thresholds and old evidence. Keep scratch in /tmp and runners in scripts/experiments/. Do not modify research-roadmap.yaml. Freeze validation commands before measurement.\n4. Declare no_model_load, MODEL_SPECS=[] and zero current model calls. Identify cached verifier work or artifact aggregation as the inference_substrate. Training small numeric heads is not an LLM load.\n5. Read the failed Exp8333 consumer_and_E2E020_021 log. All arithmetic, recovery and owned coverage gates passed; three Exp8206 assertions failed after its module fixture returned external_operand_blocked. Read-only planning localized drift in Exp8172.code_config_hashes: ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml expected sha256:004acbfa4adb4ea1ef03b2cc58f3679827c34e5b017318e2f1a2a62bb7951ba3; current manifest is sha256:ac67e6f2655c5bf4c91dee806328a04d42792a633ff2beeccc119137d4f22788. Exp8206 fixture authentication follows Exp8172 and binds this historical digest to the mutable live manifest. Reproduce that failed operand first. Authenticate its historical snapshot for old evidence; separately enforce the current manifest against this new task. Never let historical policy bypass current retirement.\n6. Fix the historical fixture input boundary, not its expected results. tests/python/test_hard_exit_learning_qualification_8206.py calls measure(e.ROOT, fixture=True), which still authenticates ambient producer operands. Supply a complete explicit private historical operand closure and versioned authority for the real consumer. Preserve every assertion, actual exits73, real coverage collection and missing-input negative control. Do not monkeypatch a passed receipt, suppress the consumer suite or promote historical evidence.\n7. Reuse Exp8333 independent dense reference, false-zero controls, 48 trajectories with64 events, and genuine process kills. Reuse bound primitive numeric evidence when unchanged; rerun only evidence affected by the repair. Require sparse/dense probability error<=1e-10, identical actions, zero stale predictions and complete durable state parity. Preserve the informational zero finding and independent rejection of a corrupted coefficient.\n8. Run the exact previously failing three cases first, then the full required consumer command and private E2E-020/021 under frozen historical operands. Qualify current authority separately. Run a negative test where the historical input is absent and confirm readiness stays zero. Set local_kernel_ready_score only after all checks pass. Write docs/research-notes/v720-local-qualification.md.\n9. Run relevant unit and consumer tests, scoped Ruff check/format, strict mypy and scripts/check_spec_coverage.py --files <owned-test-files>. Require 100 percent newly owned statements, including real CLI, child and failure paths. Use pytest -n 0 -o addopts= with private scratch. Record argv, exit, timing and log hashes. Do not run the full repository suite inside this experiment.\n10. Cold-replay primitive evidence in a fresh process. Run valid, negative and self-consistently rehashed tamper controls. Use unchanged primary_publication checks, scripts/adversarial_verify.py --json <private-candidate> and scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py --strict <private-candidate>. Keep all findings. An exit1 requires the existing typed finding consumer: only independently recomputed informational findings with deliberate-error controls can resolve. Errors, unknown severity, warnings and critical findings block readiness. Do not edit those validators or exemption lists. Publish the terminal primary atomically after checks. Owned failures are disqualified; unchanged external blocks are blocked, never partial. Reconcile openspec/, _bmad/traceability.md, ops/status.md and ops/changelog.md. Do not update generator weights or publish externally.\nREQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:\nexperiment_id, task_id, milestone, run_date: principle: Bind the invocation to its exact authority.\nhonest_verdict, verdict_class: principle: honest_verdict starts complete_. Class is positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial. Partial means retryable unfinished owned work only.\ngate_check_summary: principle: A block names upstream, path/hash, field, operator, expected and observed values. Missing is distinct from zero.\ninference_substrate, inference_substrate_class, MODEL_SPECS, model_invocation_counts, historical_model_provenance: principle: Separate current work from imported inference.\nrows, intended_count, completed_count, failed_count, censored_count, excluded_count, independent_count, sample_size_budget: principle: Retain every intended unit and condition. Repeated timings do not add independent sources.\nverifier_is_oracle, exposure_scope, independent_generalization_score, generalized_learning_benefit_score: principle: Oracle controls use circular_positive. Both generalization scores remain zero on exposed development.\nrequired_checks_passed, flagged_adversarial, acceptance_gates, validation_receipts, terminal_validation_sidecar_path, adversarial_findings: principle: Readiness requires byte-bound checks, not scientific success.\npreconditions_checked, duration_s, phase_spans, random_seed, reproducibility_checksum, source_artifact_hashes, code_config_hashes, raw_shard_hashes: principle: Bind claims to measured work and replayable inputs.\ncited_upstream_artifacts, field_principles: principle: List imported evidence and explain every added field.\nlocal_kernel_ready_score, first_failed_operand, historical_fixture_manifest, consumer_qualification: principle: A scoped fixture repair must pass the unchanged consumer assertions.\ndense_sparse_error_max, independent_dense_reference, actual_crash_receipts, finding_dispositions: principle: Keep numeric and recovery evidence distinct from natural learning benefit.\nRun command: cd {project_root} && PYTHONPATH=python:. PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 .venv/bin/python -u scripts/experiments/experiment_8347_v720_local_consumer_qualification.py --date {date}\nDo NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.", "model": "opus"}, {"id": "exp8348-continuous-local-learning", "title": "Measure delayed local learning from the already qualified sentence heads", "phase": 2, "track": "self_learning", "priority": "high", "requires_gpu": false, "max_turns": 50, "estimated_wall_time_min": 65, "per_unit_rows": true, "milestone": "2026.10.720", "deliverable": "results/experiment_8348_v720_continuous_local_learning.json", "inference_substrate_class": "no_model_load", "MODEL_SPECS": [], "gated_on": [{"upstream": "exp8346-frozen-input-contract", "artifact_field": "frozen_heads_ready_score", "op": "==", "value": 1}, {"upstream": "exp8347-local-consumer-qualification", "artifact_field": "local_kernel_ready_score", "op": "==", "value": 1}], "prior_failures": [{"experiment_id": "exp7998-selective-feedback-learning", "verdict": "complete_null_selective_feedback_learning", "addressed_by": "Use authenticated sentence-local relations and a fixed local correction objective, rather than the nine-input selectively sampled spline chain. Feedback is released uniformly after eight slots with no selection bias or inverse-propensity estimate.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}, {"experiment_id": "exp8240-qualified-delayed-learning", "verdict": "complete_null_utility_trajectory_benefit_reserved_for_8241", "addressed_by": "Replace globally supported radial/Beta utility 