branch replays. H1/H2 remain unmeasured. Preserve the frozen V717 science and historical outcomes. Cached observations are exposed development, not current model inference.\nEXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:\nCLAUDE.md; CODEX.md; ops/e2e-test-plan.md; ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml; openspec/capabilities/research-reporting/spec.md; openspec/capabilities/verification/spec.md; scripts/experiment_template.py; python/carnot/reporting/primary_publication.py; openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md; openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-v719-preserved-20261009.md; openspec/change-proposals/v717-local-learning-protocol.json; results/experiment_8334_v719_sentence_spline_fit.json; python/carnot/verify/sparse_energy_7996.py; python/carnot/verify/dependency_scoped_admission_8291.py; python/carnot/verify/calibrated_memory_trajectory_8211.py; results/experiment_7998_v693_selective_feedback_learning.json; results/experiment_8240_v712_qualified_delayed_learning.json; openspec/capabilities/self-learning/spec.md\nTASK:\nMeasure delayed local learning from the already qualified sentence heads. Deliver results/experiment_8348_v720_continuous_local_learning.json. Create the thin runner scripts/experiments/experiment_8348_v720_continuous_local_learning.py. Store primitive evidence under results/raw/experiment_8348_v720_continuous_local_learning/. Future deliverables are dependencies, not existing inputs.\nCONCRETE STEPS:\n1. PRECONDITIONS: Emit a flushed start line. Authenticate source bytes, terminal sidecars and task authority. Check private scratch, tools and resources before work. Name missing external operands in gate_check_summary. Do not replace natural evidence with fixtures.\n2. Emit a flushed progress line at every phase boundary. Emit one before and after every model load, generation, benchmark and subprocess. Print completed/pending counts inside long loops. Poll owned children at least every 60 seconds. Use unbuffered output and bounded deadlines. Keep every silence gap below 600 seconds. Write files over about 200 lines in several tool calls of at most about 150 lines. Send a progress message between calls. No single huge tool call. Do not pad elapsed time.\n3. Spec first: add relevant REQ-* and SCENARIO-* before implementation. Write focused failing tests first. Reuse existing modules through small adapters. Preserve assertions, guard thresholds and old evidence. Keep scratch in /tmp and runners in scripts/experiments/. Do not modify research-roadmap.yaml. Freeze validation commands before measurement.\n4. Declare no_model_load, MODEL_SPECS=[] and zero current model calls. Identify cached verifier work or artifact aggregation as the inference_substrate. Training small numeric heads is not an LLM load.\n5. Authenticate Exp8346.frozen_heads_ready_score and Exp8347.local_kernel_ready_score. Load the exact original Exp8334 checkpoint named by Exp8346. The new input receipt does not contain replacement weights. Require no new static fitting and no H1-result gate.\n6. Seal all online issue rows and retention-window predictions before Exp8350 or Exp8351 opens evaluator targets. Expose only due stream labels through the release API. Include a mutation test that changes future labels and leaves all prior decisions unchanged.\n7. Declare no_model_load, inference_substrate=verifier_ensemble_against_cached_candidates, MODEL_SPECS=[] and generator_weight_updates=0. This is Tier1 continuous online learning on replayed natural observations, with Tier2 durable state; it is not autonomous acquisition of new semantic constraint types.\n8. Read only fit/tune-trained checkpoints and the stream96 predictor shard. Start each arm from the same frozen spline head. Arms: frozen_spline, online_sparse, mathematically identical online_dense, calibration_only (intercept update only), and shuffled_due_feedback negative control (seed7178310, draw with replacement only from labels already released at that slot; never build a permutation from future feedback). All arms receive the same available due feedback; no acceptance-selected labeling or future labels.\n9. For slot t, issue and durably record every arm's prediction and state hash FIRST; then release only the label from slot t-8. Apply at most one stable logistic SGD step with learning rate.01, active-coefficient gradient norm cap1 and coordinate bounds[-4,4]. Online sparse/dense freeze the intercept, temperature, holistic slope and knots; only active spline coordinates change. Use derivative of the deployed temperature-scaled logit. No online L2 decay, future-driven refit or parameter search. Before the natural trajectory, use a separate fit-only control with the exact <=88-update budget to demonstrate a typed-action crossing; record attainable logit-change bounds and starting margins for every real source. This diagnostic cannot retune the method. Failure limits interpretation to an update-budget null, not evidence that natural learning is impossible. Calibration-only uses the same clipping/step budget but updates its intercept.\n10. Index cached unissued predictions by actual active coefficients; reject duplicate/stale feedback IDs, preserve hard invariants, and use full recomputation when metadata is incomplete. Issued decisions never change after release. Missing source features imply escalation and no parameter update. Persist coefficients, pending issues, feedback IDs and index version before acknowledging a release.\n11. Use the frozen source order, delay8 and no cohort replacement. Kill owned children after durable updates at slots32/64, resume, and compare all semantic state and issued predictions against an uninterrupted run. Future-label mutation must not change earlier decisions; the sparse/dense paths must remain within1e-10 with identical typed decisions. Preserve out-of-support and global-invalidation rows.\n12. For each admitted change, record its source, basis support, coefficient delta and whether a LATER distinct source's probability/action changed. Produce shadow predictions on the retention32 features at windows0/32/64/96 without opening retention targets. Measure memory bytes and complete durable-update latency; learning benefit is reserved for Exp8351.\n13. Set trajectory_ready_score only on issue/release causality, exact restart, complete accounting and passed checks. Self-learning may qualify mechanically with zero decision gain. Store raw issued/update/checkpoint/retention events under the declared raw directory and write docs/research-notes/v720-learning-trajectory.md.\n14. Run relevant unit and consumer tests, scoped Ruff check/format, strict mypy and scripts/check_spec_coverage.py --files <owned-test-files>. Require 100 percent newly owned statements, including real CLI, child and failure paths. Use pytest -n 0 -o addopts= with private scratch. Record argv, exit, timing and log hashes. Do not run the full repository suite inside this experiment.\n15. Cold-replay primitive evidence in a fresh process. Run valid, negative and self-consistently rehashed tamper controls. Use unchanged primary_publication checks, scripts/adversarial_verify.py --json <private-candidate> and scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py --strict <private-candidate>. Keep all findings. An exit1 requires the existing typed finding consumer: only independently recomputed informational findings with deliberate-error controls can resolve. Errors, unknown severity, warnings and critical findings block readiness. Do not edit those validators or exemption lists. Publish the terminal primary atomically after checks. Owned failures are disqualified; unchanged external blocks are blocked, never partial. Reconcile openspec/, _bmad/traceability.md, ops/status.md and ops/changelog.md. Do not update generator weights or publish externally.\nREQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:\nexperiment_id, task_id, milestone, run_date: principle: Bind the invocation to its exact authority.\nhonest_verdict, verdict_class: principle: honest_verdict starts complete_. Class is positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial. Partial means retryable unfinished owned work only.\ngate_check_summary: principle: A block names upstream, path/hash, field, operator, expected and observed values. Missing is distinct from zero.\ninference_substrate, inference_substrate_class, MODEL_SPECS, model_invocation_counts, historical_model_provenance: principle: Separate current work from imported inference.\nrows, intended_count, completed_count, failed_count, censored_count, excluded_count, independent_count, sample_size_budget: principle: Retain every intended unit and condition. Repeated timings do not add independent sources.\nverifier_is_oracle, exposure_scope, independent_generalization_score, generalized_learning_benefit_score: principle: Oracle controls use circular_positive. Both generalization scores remain zero on exposed development.\nrequired_checks_passed, flagged_adversarial, acceptance_gates, validation_receipts, terminal_validation_sidecar_path, adversarial_findings: principle: Readiness requires byte-bound checks, not scientific success.\npreconditions_checked, duration_s, phase_spans, random_seed, reproducibility_checksum, source_artifact_hashes, code_config_hashes, raw_shard_hashes: principle: Bind claims to measured work and replayable inputs.\ncited_upstream_artifacts, field_principles: principle: List imported evidence and explain every added field.\nheads_sha256, trajectory_ready_score, issued_rows, update_rows, retention_prediction_seals: principle: Predictions precede delayed feedback; all retention windows seal before target access.\nupdate_budget_control, reachable_action_rows, crash_replay_rows, later_source_attribution: principle: Parameter movement alone is not useful learning.\nRun command: cd {project_root} && PYTHONPATH=python:. PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 .venv/bin/python -u scripts/experiments/experiment_8348_v720_continuous_local_learning.py --date {date}\nDo NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.", "model": "sonnet"}, {"id": "exp8349-bounded-feedback-capacity", "title": "Measure finite feedback tracking with persistent admission and loss", "phase": 2, "track": "self_learning", "priority": "high", "requires_gpu": false, "max_turns": 50, "estimated_wall_time_min": 55, "per_unit_rows": true, "milestone": "2026.10.720", "deliverable": "results/experiment_8349_v720_bounded_feedback_capacity.json", "inference_substrate_class": "no_model_load", "MODEL_SPECS": [], "gated_on": [{"upstream": "exp8347-local-consumer-qualification", "artifact_field": "local_kernel_ready_score", "op": "==", "value": 1}], "prior_failures": [{"experiment_id": "exp8306-local-update-isolation", "verdict": "complete_disqualified_owned_checks", "addressed_by": "Use current qualified numerical evidence and a separate capacity/lost-feedback question. The prior study tested locality and crashes without a hard pending-memory bound.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}, {"experiment_id": "exp8323-bounded-feedback-capacity", "verdict": "GATE_BLOCK (producer absent)", "addressed_by": "The constructed capacity producer was absent after an unrelated historical gate skipped kernel qualification. It now depends only on the independently qualified local kernel.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}, {"experiment_id": "exp8337-bounded-feedback-capacity", "verdict": "blocked_gate_check_failed", "addressed_by": "The prior task never ran because local qualification failed its consumer fixture. Exp8347 repairs that operand boundary; the finite-capacity question is unchanged.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}], "prompt": "CONTEXT:\nWork in {project_root} on {date}. V719 wrote nine producer primaries and three conductor pre-gate receipts; two producer slots have neither. Static heads and reserved predictions qualified (Exp8334/8335). Local qualification failed three Exp8206 consumer assertions; runtime failed two Exp8307 authority assertions; ARC failed strict typing; cost consumers failed three Exp8329 assertions. GateMate history drifted. The capstone passed its memory checks but failed two branch replays. H1/H2 remain unmeasured. Preserve the frozen V717 science and historical outcomes. Cached observations are exposed development, not current model inference.\nEXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:\nCLAUDE.md; CODEX.md; ops/e2e-test-plan.md; ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml; openspec/capabilities/research-reporting/spec.md; openspec/capabilities/verification/spec.md; scripts/experiment_template.py; python/carnot/reporting/primary_publication.py; openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md; openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-v719-preserved-20261009.md; openspec/change-proposals/v717-local-learning-protocol.json; python/carnot/verify/local_update_isolation_8306.py; python/carnot/verify/hard_exit_learning_qualification_8206.py; results/experiment_8306_v717_local_update_isolation.json; research-references.md\nTASK:\nMeasure finite feedback tracking with persistent admission and loss. Deliver results/experiment_8349_v720_bounded_feedback_capacity.json. Create the thin runner scripts/experiments/experiment_8349_v720_bounded_feedback_capacity.py. Store primitive evidence under results/raw/experiment_8349_v720_bounded_feedback_capacity/. Future deliverables are dependencies, not existing inputs.\nCONCRETE STEPS:\n1. PRECONDITIONS: Emit a flushed start line. Authenticate source bytes, terminal sidecars and task authority. Check private scratch, tools and resources before work. Name missing external operands in gate_check_summary. Do not replace natural evidence with fixtures.\n2. Emit a flushed progress line at every phase boundary. Emit one before and after every model load, generation, benchmark and subprocess. Print completed/pending counts inside long loops. Poll owned children at least every 60 seconds. Use unbuffered output and bounded deadlines. Keep every silence gap below 600 seconds. Write files over about 200 lines in several tool calls of at most about 150 lines. Send a progress message between calls. No single huge tool call. Do not pad elapsed time.\n3. Spec first: add relevant REQ-* and SCENARIO-* before implementation. Write focused failing tests first. Reuse existing modules through small adapters. Preserve assertions, guard thresholds and old evidence. Keep scratch in /tmp and runners in scripts/experiments/. Do not modify research-roadmap.yaml. Freeze validation commands before measurement.\n4. Declare no_model_load, MODEL_SPECS=[] and zero current model calls. Identify cached verifier work or artifact aggregation as the inference_substrate. Training small numeric heads is not an LLM load.\n5. Authenticate Exp8347.local_kernel_ready_score. Capacity testing does not depend on natural H2 success. Freeze all constructed traces and scheduler rules before observations. Count only three trace families as independent constructed workloads.\n6. Freeze three512-event constructed trajectories before running. Use slots t=1..512. Local input j=0..3 is ((17*t+13*j)%101)/100. Put these in x[12:16] and set other16-dimensional features to0. Set y=1 when s*(2*x[12]-x[13]+x[14]-2*x[15]+.1)>=0; s=1 through256 and-1 afterward. These are constructed labels, never natural annotations. Delays are constant8, repeating[1,8,32,64], or64 during slots129..256 and8 otherwise. Expose a delay only when it expires. The evaluator retains lost labels; the learner cannot read them.\n7. Compare unlimited tracking, first-admit/no-preemption, and admission by a fixed random priority at capacities4/16/64. At each issue draw an independent continuous priority; keep the C smallest among pending items and the new issue. A dropped item permanently loses learner feedback. Log priorities and membership, not invented marginal retention probabilities. Do not use inverse-propensity weighting: retention depends on future competition. This is a systems adaptation, not the paper scheduler or DW-FTRL. Compare sparse and dense implementations on identical retained labels. Reuse frozen basis and step.01, cap1; initialize all coefficients0, slope1, intercept0,T1. Log every issue, drop, due event and update.\n8. For each tick, issue prediction and admission before processing due labels. This ordering makes capacity64 insufficient for a full64-delay pipeline at its boundary; preserve that effect. After slot512, drain eligible feedback without scoring additional predictions. Run capacities on three traces and seeds11/22/33. Seeds randomize admission only; there are three constructed traces, not27 independent natural datasets.\n9. Measure maximum pending count, feedback retained/lost, log loss, typed-action cost, coefficient touches, bytes written and full update time. Require count<=C at every tick. Kill after durable state at128/256 and resume with identical random-generator state and semantic output. Negative controls include future-label leakage, lost-label resurrection and capacity overflow.\n10. Publish all unit rows and descriptive contrasts. A passing systems gate requires every capacity/order/restart invariant and a deliberate-overflow control that fails. No requirement that random admission beats first-admit. Set capacity_ready_score from invariants only. A utility difference is constructed evidence, never a natural learning benefit. Run private E2E-020 recovery checks.\n11. Run relevant unit and consumer tests, scoped Ruff check/format, strict mypy and scripts/check_spec_coverage.py --files <owned-test-files>. Require 100 percent newly owned statements, including real CLI, child and failure paths. Use pytest -n 0 -o addopts= with private scratch. Record argv, exit, timing and log hashes. Do not run the full repository suite inside this experiment.\n12. Cold-replay primitive evidence in a fresh process. Run valid, negative and self-consistently rehashed tamper controls. Use unchanged primary_publication checks, scripts/adversarial_verify.py --json <private-candidate> and scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py --strict <private-candidate>. Keep all findings. An exit1 requires the existing typed finding consumer: only independently recomputed informational findings with deliberate-error controls can resolve. Errors, unknown severity, warnings and critical findings block readiness. Do not edit those validators or exemption lists. Publish the terminal primary atomically after checks. Owned failures are disqualified; unchanged external blocks are blocked, never partial. Reconcile openspec/, _bmad/traceability.md, ops/status.md and ops/changelog.md. Do not update generator weights or publish externally.\nREQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:\nexperiment_id, task_id, milestone, run_date: principle: Bind the invocation to its exact authority.\nhonest_verdict, verdict_class: principle: honest_verdict starts complete_. Class is positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial. Partial means retryable unfinished owned work only.\ngate_check_summary: principle: A block names upstream, path/hash, field, operator, expected and observed values. Missing is distinct from zero.\ninference_substrate, inference_substrate_class, MODEL_SPECS, model_invocation_counts, historical_model_provenance: principle: Separate current work from imported inference.\nrows, intended_count, completed_count, failed_count, censored_count, excluded_count, independent_count, sample_size_budget: principle: Retain every intended unit and condition. Repeated timings do not add independent sources.\nverifier_is_oracle, exposure_scope, independent_generalization_score, generalized_learning_benefit_score: principle: Oracle controls use circular_positive. Both generalization scores remain zero on exposed development.\nrequired_checks_passed, flagged_adversarial, acceptance_gates, validation_receipts, terminal_validation_sidecar_path, adversarial_findings: principle: Readiness requires byte-bound checks, not scientific success.\npreconditions_checked, duration_s, phase_spans, random_seed, reproducibility_checksum, source_artifact_hashes, code_config_hashes, raw_shard_hashes: principle: Bind claims to measured work and replayable inputs.\ncited_upstream_artifacts, field_principles: principle: List imported evidence and explain every added field.\ncapacity_ready_score, per_event_rows, maximum_pending_count, feedback_retained, feedback_lost: principle: Every tick proves the capacity and causal release rules.\nscheduler_rng_state, crash_replay_rows, trace_family_count, constructed_utility_rows: principle: Recovery includes scheduler state; constructed utility is not natural improvement.\nRun command: cd {project_root} && PYTHONPATH=python:. PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 .venv/bin/python -u scripts/experiments/experiment_8349_v720_bounded_feedback_capacity.py --date {date}\nDo NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.", "model": "sonnet"}, {"id": "exp8350-static-benefit-audit", "title": "Audit sealed static decisions while preserving every retention-label barrier", "phase": 2, "track": "evaluation", "priority": "high", "requires_gpu": false, "max_turns": 50, "estimated_wall_time_min": 45, "per_unit_rows": true, "milestone": "2026.10.720", "deliverable": "results/experiment_8350_v720_static_benefit_audit.json", "inference_substrate_class": "no_model_load", "MODEL_SPECS": [], "gated_on": [{"upstream": "exp8346-frozen-input-contract", "artifact_field": "frozen_predictions_ready_score", "op": "==", "value": 1}], "prior_failures": [{"experiment_id": "exp8185-sentence-decision-audit", "verdict": "complete_null_sentence_decision_null", "addressed_by": "Audit the frozen local spline representation against a comparator selected on separate tune slots. No new evidence or generalization is claimed; a same-mechanism null retires this four-feature static head.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}, {"experiment_id": "exp7428-decision-audit", "verdict": "complete_null_static_and_online_audits_reproduce_no_registered_benefit", "addressed_by": "The current inputs include authenticated Qwen sentence relations, absent from the earlier lexical/scalar spline study; report earlier negative evidence explicitly.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}, {"experiment_id": "exp8311-static-benefit-audit", "verdict": "GATE_BLOCK (producer absent)", "addressed_by": "The prior static and online seals were absent. Require current complete seals, then run the unchanged H1 audit; this is first measurement, not a null rerun.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}, {"experiment_id": "exp8324-static-benefit-audit", "verdict": "GATE_BLOCK (producer absent)", "addressed_by": "No audit producer existed because prediction producers were skipped. Use both current immutable seals; a missing seal remains blocked, never a scientific null.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}, {"experiment_id": "exp8338-static-benefit-audit", "verdict": "blocked_gate_check_failed", "addressed_by": "Static predictions now exist. Replace preemptive online cascade gating with an unconditional seal-aware reader; missing retention seals still block full H1 and never authorize target leakage.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}], "prompt": "CONTEXT:\nWork in {project_root} on {date}. V719 wrote nine producer primaries and three conductor pre-gate receipts; two producer slots have neither. Static heads and reserved predictions qualified (Exp8334/8335). Local qualification failed three Exp8206 consumer assertions; runtime failed two Exp8307 authority assertions; ARC failed strict typing; cost consumers failed three Exp8329 assertions. GateMate history drifted. The capstone passed its memory checks but failed two branch replays. H1/H2 remain unmeasured. Preserve the frozen V717 science and historical outcomes. Cached observations are exposed development, not current model inference.\nEXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:\nCLAUDE.md; CODEX.md; ops/e2e-test-plan.md; ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml; openspec/capabilities/research-reporting/spec.md; openspec/capabilities/verification/spec.md; scripts/experiment_template.py; python/carnot/reporting/primary_publication.py; openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md; openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-v719-preserved-20261009.md; openspec/change-proposals/v717-local-learning-protocol.json; results/experiment_8335_v719_reserved_prediction_seal.json; python/carnot/verify/sentence_decision_audit_8185.py; results/experiment_8185_v707_sentence_decision_audit.json; results/experiment_7428_v651_decision_audit.json; scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py\nTASK:\nAudit sealed static decisions while preserving every retention-label barrier. Deliver results/experiment_8350_v720_static_benefit_audit.json. Create the thin runner scripts/experiments/experiment_8350_v720_static_benefit_audit.py. Store primitive evidence under results/raw/experiment_8350_v720_static_benefit_audit/. Future deliverables are dependencies, not existing inputs.\nCONCRETE STEPS:\n1. PRECONDITIONS: Emit a flushed start line. Authenticate source bytes, terminal sidecars and task authority. Check private scratch, tools and resources before work. Name missing external operands in gate_check_summary. Do not replace natural evidence with fixtures.\n2. Emit a flushed progress line at every phase boundary. Emit one before and after every model load, generation, benchmark and subprocess. Print completed/pending counts inside long loops. Poll owned children at least every 60 seconds. Use unbuffered output and bounded deadlines. Keep every silence gap below 600 seconds. Write files over about 200 lines in several tool calls of at most about 150 lines. Send a progress message between calls. No single huge tool call. Do not pad elapsed time.\n3. Spec first: add relevant REQ-* and SCENARIO-* before implementation. Write focused failing tests first. Reuse existing modules through small adapters. Preserve assertions, guard thresholds and old evidence. Keep scratch in /tmp and runners in scripts/experiments/. Do not modify research-roadmap.yaml. Freeze validation commands before measurement.\n4. Declare no_model_load, MODEL_SPECS=[] and zero current model calls. Identify cached verifier work or artifact aggregation as the inference_substrate. Training small numeric heads is not an LLM load.\n5. Authenticate Exp8346.frozen_predictions_ready_score and the original Exp8335 seal. There is no conductor gate on online success. Before opening ANY reserved target, inspect Exp8348 retention seals. If all windows are sealed, run the unchanged full H1 audit. If they are absent, keep retention targets sealed and leave H1 unmeasured. In this blocked path emit predictor-only action counts and margins on the first96 stream slots. Open no reserved targets at all. Label this a predictor-only diagnostic; never score utility or apply the128-slot H1 threshold to it. Set static_audit_ready_score=0 and verdict_class=blocked for the missing full-H1 seal. Do not retune H2 from this diagnostic.\n6. Use no_model_load, inference_substrate=aggregation_from_upstream_artifacts and MODEL_SPECS=[]. Open the evaluator shard only after authenticating Exp8346's static seal and Exp8348's complete learning and four-window retention seals. Targets may be read by this audit after all learner outputs are immutable; no target feedback enters the learner from this audit. Independently reduce rows rather than importing upstream means.\n7. H1 primary: mean intended-slot cost(selected comparator)-cost(spline34) across128 reserved sources. Missing features use the same escalation and .5 cost for all arms; unresolved targets cannot establish a correct accept/reject and receive explicit bounds. Report paired complete-case and all-intended results, Brier/log loss on qualified labels, risk at achieved coverage, and counts of changed decisions.\n8. Use10000 source-cluster bootstrap resamples with seed7178311 and nominal one-sided97.5 percent lower bound. These are descriptive development intervals because the cohort is already exposed; alpha=.025 is a frozen reporting threshold, not a fresh confirmatory test. Require >=80 qualified sources, >=8 per binary label, a working typed-action positive control and positive permissible-action oracle headroom before calling a scientific null informative.\n9. A representation-level informative null also requires the exact optimizer positive control and meaningful optimization residuals; otherwise classify optimization-limited evidence. A development signal requires mean cost gain>=.02, lower bound>0 and Brier degradation<=.01 versus the preselected comparator. Also show frozen-holistic, linear6, scalar2 and RBF34 results with no post-hoc comparator substitution. Equal-input gains over RBF concern the frozen training procedures; only qualified optimization can further support a geometry interpretation. Neither establishes independent truth, and sigmoid34 parity precludes energy-specific novelty.\n10. Audit input independence by varying withheld targets, source IDs and feature masks without changing issued predictions; run a label-only forbidden-feature control that must fail. Record all denominators and per-source paired costs. Set static_audit_ready_score=1 for a valid audit even when H1 is null; scientific support insufficiency is null_insufficient_support, while missing external artifacts are blocked.\n11. Write docs/research-notes/v720-static-benefit.md. Do not choose new features, knots, thresholds, role splits or samples after viewing these results. H1 cannot gate the online task.\n12. Run relevant unit and consumer tests, scoped Ruff check/format, strict mypy and scripts/check_spec_coverage.py --files <owned-test-files>. Require 100 percent newly owned statements, including real CLI, child and failure paths. Use pytest -n 0 -o addopts= with private scratch. Record argv, exit, timing and log hashes. Do not run the full repository suite inside this experiment.\n13. Cold-replay primitive evidence in a fresh process. Run valid, negative and self-consistently rehashed tamper controls. Use unchanged primary_publication checks, scripts/adversarial_verify.py --json <private-candidate> and scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py --strict <private-candidate>. Keep all findings. An exit1 requires the existing typed finding consumer: only independently recomputed informational findings with deliberate-error controls can resolve. Errors, unknown severity, warnings and critical findings block readiness. Do not edit those validators or exemption lists. Publish the terminal primary atomically after checks. Owned failures are disqualified; unchanged external blocks are blocked, never partial. Reconcile openspec/, _bmad/traceability.md, ops/status.md and ops/changelog.md. Do not update generator weights or publish externally.\nREQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:\nexperiment_id, task_id, milestone, run_date: principle: Bind the invocation to its exact authority.\nhonest_verdict, verdict_class: principle: honest_verdict starts complete_. Class is positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial. Partial means retryable unfinished owned work only.\ngate_check_summary: principle: A block names upstream, path/hash, field, operator, expected and observed values. Missing is distinct from zero.\ninference_substrate, inference_substrate_class, MODEL_SPECS, model_invocation_counts, historical_model_provenance: principle: Separate current work from imported inference.\nrows, intended_count, completed_count, failed_count, censored_count, excluded_count, independent_count, sample_size_budget: principle: Retain every intended unit and condition. Repeated timings do not add independent sources.\nverifier_is_oracle, exposure_scope, independent_generalization_score, generalized_learning_benefit_score: principle: Oracle controls use circular_positive. Both generalization scores remain zero on exposed development.\nrequired_checks_passed, flagged_adversarial, acceptance_gates, validation_receipts, terminal_validation_sidecar_path, adversarial_findings: principle: Readiness requires byte-bound checks, not scientific success.\npreconditions_checked, duration_s, phase_spans, random_seed, reproducibility_checksum, source_artifact_hashes, code_config_hashes, raw_shard_hashes: principle: Bind claims to measured work and replayable inputs.\ncited_upstream_artifacts, field_principles: principle: List imported evidence and explain every added field.\nstatic_audit_ready_score, h1_development_signal_score, full_h1_measured, stream_diagnostic_only: principle: A stream diagnostic cannot substitute for the frozen128-slot H1.\nretention_seal_check, label_access_log, comparator_id, paired_cost_rows, bootstrap_summary, missing_bounds: principle: Verify target access and reduce all intended units independently.\nRun command: cd {project_root} && PYTHONPATH=python:. PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 .venv/bin/python -u scripts/experiments/experiment_8350_v720_static_benefit_audit.py --date {date}\nDo NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.", "model": "sonnet"}, {"id": "exp8351-learning-retention-audit", "title": "Audit later decision utility and all fixed retention windows", "phase": 2, "track": "evaluation", "priority": "high", "requires_gpu": false, "max_turns": 50, "estimated_wall_time_min": 45, "per_unit_rows": true, "milestone": "2026.10.720", "deliverable": "results/experiment_8351_v720_learning_retention_audit.json", "inference_substrate_class": "no_model_load", "MODEL_SPECS": [], "gated_on": [{"upstream": "exp8348-continuous-local-learning", "artifact_field": "trajectory_ready_score", "op": "==", "value": 1}], "prior_failures": [{"experiment_id": "exp7999-learning-causal-audit", "verdict": "complete_null_learning_causal_audit", "addressed_by": "Reduce the new uniformly delayed local-feature trajectory and exact sparse/dense control instead of the earlier selective-feedback trajectory.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}, {"experiment_id": "exp8241-delayed-benefit-audit", "verdict": "complete_null_delayed_decision_benefit", "addressed_by": "Test a changed local parameter-update mechani