or database durability. No invented Ising encoding or projected speedup. Only run a bounded board transcript if an authenticated compatible kernel exists. Otherwise retain a precise blocked FPGA execution obligation.\n9. Authenticate Exp8259 PolarFire primary, sidecars, dispatch hash and output parity. Its graduated terminal scope is board-local Linux CPU, not FPGA fabric. A failed check becomes an unmet obligation; do not perform a redundant physical probe. TSU and NPU remain unqualified.\n10. Write docs/research-notes/v720-hardware-cost-boundary.md. Keep arithmetic_cost_ready_score, durable_cost_ready_score and kv260_execution_ready_score separate. Derive a complete-service Amdahl bound only if every service component and compatible fraction is measured. Otherwise report null bounds. Run private E2E-018/020 for exercised branches.\n11. Run relevant unit and consumer tests, scoped Ruff check/format, strict mypy and scripts/check_spec_coverage.py --files <owned-test-files>. Require 100 percent newly owned statements, including real CLI, child and failure paths. Use pytest -n 0 -o addopts= with private scratch. Record argv, exit, timing and log hashes. Do not run the full repository suite inside this experiment.\n12. Cold-replay primitive evidence in a fresh process. Run valid, negative and self-consistently rehashed tamper controls. Use unchanged primary_publication checks, scripts/adversarial_verify.py --json <private-candidate> and scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py --strict <private-candidate>. Keep all findings. An exit1 requires the existing typed finding consumer: only independently recomputed informational findings with deliberate-error controls can resolve. Errors, unknown severity, warnings and critical findings block readiness. Do not edit those validators or exemption lists. Publish the terminal primary atomically after checks. Owned failures are disqualified; unchanged external blocks are blocked, never partial. Reconcile openspec/, _bmad/traceabili